# The .editorconfig asks for `end_of_line = lf`, and Directory.Build.props turns
# a formatting warning into a build error (TreatWarningsAsErrors +
# EnforceCodeStyleInBuild). Without this, GitHub's Windows runner checks out
# CRLF -- core.autocrlf=true is the default there -- and IDE0055 fails the
# build on every line. That is why CI's windows job failed on Build for weeks
# while linux passed: nothing to do with the code, only with how it arrived.
# Reproduced by converting two files to CRLF locally: the same lines GitHub
# annotated came back (2026-09-21).
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the exception. A batch file with LF endings can mis-parse, and
# akuwm-rescue.cmd is what a person runs when everything else is broken.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
